As a longtime addict, initially of the mild drug called "Rogue" then of
the harder drug called "Hack" and now on the totally addictive "NetHack",
I would like to propose a socially redemptive (optional) enhancement to
this game/drug/lifestyle:

An additional class of monsters (we've all come in contact with them)
called teachers/instructors/professors.  This class of monster would be
immune to all forms of attack and would block any form of progress to
lower (i.e. _higher_) levels until one or more multiple choice questions
were answered correctly.  Certain items of apparel (helm of learning,
morterboard, black robe with purple shawl, etc.), and artifacts (scroll
of graduation, spellbook of spelling, etc.) could be integrated in a
manner that didn't "kludge" the mainstream character of the game.

Questions (with answers) could be encrypted in external files in a 
variety of topics, and provided by a variety of addicted monsters in the
"real" world.  One could then "hook" one's kids on the game ....
without guilt (?)   ..... "Say know to NetHack"?

It seems to me this would (in certain circles) provide some social
redemption fopr the hours spent attempting to sate one's depedency.

